    67	 *
    68	 * Admitting all of `M` was caught within one test run by the fixtures already in this file: U+FE0F
    69	 * VARIATION SELECTOR-16 is `Mn` and renders NOTHING — it modifies a neighbour's presentation. Widening
    70	 * by category alone would have re-opened the original hole through a side door.
    71	 *
    72	 * `Default_Ignorable_Code_Point` is the standard's own answer to "renders as nothing", so the rule is:
    73	 * a letter, number, punctuation mark, symbol or mark is content UNLESS the standard says it is
    74	 * ignorable. One principled subtraction from a positive base, not a hand-list of exceptions.
    75	 */
    76	const IGNORABLE_RE = /\p{Default_Ignorable_Code_Point}/u;
    77	
    78	/**
    79	 * Code points that are CATEGORY-POSITIVE but render BLANK — the positive predicate's own false positives.
    80	 *
    81	 * Found at convergence round 10, and confirmed by execution: each of these is a letter (`Lo`) or a symbol
    82	 * (`So`) by General_Category, so `CONTENT_RE` accepted it, and each renders as empty space in ordinary
    83	 * clients. A message of one HANGUL FILLER is the incident all over again, wearing a letter's category.
    84	 *
    85	 * **Honest about what this is.** The positive definition closed the open world of non-printing CATEGORIES;
    86	 * this is a small subtraction from inside the positive set, and a subtraction has a tail — a future
    87	 * category-positive blank code point would pass until it is added here. That residual is accepted
    88	 * deliberately and stated in the spec rather than papered over: the structural fix is the vendored,
    89	 * generated table (CMT-1261 — it was CMT-1246 criterion (d), which shipped without it), which derives blankness rather than listing it. Fixtures pin every member.
    90	 */
    91	const BLANK_GLYPHS = new Set([
    92	  'ㅤ',  // HANGUL FILLER (Lo)
    93	  'ᅟ',  // HANGUL CHOSEONG FILLER (Lo)
    94	  'ᅠ',  // HANGUL JUNGSEONG FILLER (Lo)
    95	  'ﾠ',  // HALFWIDTH HANGUL FILLER (Lo)
    96	  '⠀',  // BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK (So)
    97	]);
