    99	/**
   100	 * True when `text` carries nothing a reader could receive as content. Callers refuse such a payload
   101	 * rather than sending it.
   102	 *
   103	 * The name is kept for its callers and its history; the precise claim is the MECHANICALLY-VISIBLE one:
   104	 * the string contains at least one letter, number, punctuation mark, symbol OR MARK that is not
   105	 * `Default_Ignorable` and not a known blank glyph. (Corrected at review pass 33 finding 5: this
   106	 * sentence still listed only L/N/P/S after marks were admitted — the account of a repair going stale
   107	 * one function below the repair itself.)
