docs/specs/reports/telegram-markdown-renderer-convergence.md:19:**The original spec** (iteration 0) assumed instar sent all Telegram messages as `parse_mode: 'HTML'` and said "every send path goes through one `sendMessage` method, so we intercept there." Both of those premises were wrong. The real state is: instar sends mostly as `parse_mode: 'Markdown'` (legacy Markdown), ONE callsite already uses HTML, and send paths flow through two separate `apiCall()` methods (one in `TelegramAdapter`, one in `TelegramLifeline` — different class, different Bot API client, same token). That alone would have broken the feature on deployment.
